\section*{Global Arthur enhancements of occurring excursion parameters}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 014; 2026-10-05), the asserted result is that assuming the stated finite-level decomposition, each occurring cuspidal excursion parameter for a split semisimple function-field group has a global Arthur enhancement with one algebraic $\mathrm{SL}_2$ and a commuting Weil action, including inertia.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Manuscript 1.}
Let $X/\mathbb F_q$ be smooth projective geometrically connected, $G/\mathbb F_q$ split connected semisimple, $D$ an effective divisor, $U=X\setminus\operatorname{supp}D$ and $K_D=\ker(G(\mathcal O_{\mathbb A})\to G(\mathcal O_D))$. Fix $\ell\ne\operatorname{char}\mathbb F_q$, $k=\overline{\mathbb Q}_{\ell}$, an embedding $j:\overline{\mathbb Q}\to k$ and $a=j(\sqrt q)$. For an occurring character $\nu$ of the excursion algebra on cuspidal functions at full level $K_D$, write $\sigma_{\nu}:\pi_1(U)\to\widehat G(k)$ for its parameter and $\Gamma=W_U$ for the Weil subgroup.

The theorem assumes the companion finite-level decomposition: one nilpotent orbit $\mathcal O_{\nu}$ works at all good points, and each semisimple Frobenius class has the form $[\phi_{\mathcal O_{\nu}}(\operatorname{diag}(a^{d_x},a^{-d_x}))c_x]$, with $c_x$ commuting, algebraic and compact at every complex embedding. Under this assumption it claims a global algebraic $\phi_{\nu}:\operatorname{SL}_2\to\widehat G$ and continuous $\tau_{\nu}:\Gamma\to Z_{\widehat G}(\phi_{\nu}(\operatorname{SL}_2))(k)$, defined over a finite $\ell$-adic extension, with reductive Zariski closure, such that after one fixed conjugation
\[
 \sigma_{\nu}(w)=\tau_{\nu}(w)\phi_{\nu}(\operatorname{diag}(a^{\deg w},a^{-\deg w}))\quad(w\in\Gamma).
\]
The differential of $\phi_{\nu}$ sends the standard upper nilpotent matrix into $\mathcal O_{\nu}$. For every rational-form algebraic representation and closed $x\in U$, eigenvalues of $\tau_{\nu}(\operatorname{Frob}_x)$ are algebraic and have absolute value one at every complex embedding. The full centralizer may be disconnected. Ellipticity, packet classification and a multiplicity formula are not asserted.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 014; 2026-10-05), shtuka cohomology supplies a finite-type cyclic support carrying full excursion data. Frobenius-compatible coherent models of Iwahori categories at several places identify an open-orbit condition, which assembles a single commuting Weil and $\mathrm{SL}_2$ pair.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 014; 2026-10-05).

\subsection{Formal verification}
No Lean formalization is listed at this snapshot for manuscript 1 (family 014; 2026-10-05).

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

\subsection{Status caveat}
The manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model. OpenAI cautions that results without formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently checked the proofs; the label records the scope of OpenAI's claim.

